{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They scatter knowledge</b> — that they teach it to the simpletons." "<b>But the heart of fools is not so</b> — he [the fool] does not know how to scatter knowledge as the wise do, i.e., 'not so'; and this is the correct interpretation."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra offers two readings of לא כן: either the fool does teach but not as the wise do, or he does not know how to scatter knowledge at all; he endorses the latter. The syntax of the first option is compressed and ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:57.885530868Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}